# Non-secret deploy-time configuration for Cloud Functions.
#
# Committed on purpose: firebase-functions reads this at deploy to resolve
# defineString() params, so a deploy from a fresh clone needs it present. Real
# secrets live in Secret Manager (functions:secrets:set) and never appear here.

# Whose data the MCP server serves. Not a secret, but it is the whole
# authorization model: the bearer token proves the caller may act, this says
# who they act as. Configuration rather than input, so no tool call can change
# it. Find it in the Firebase console under Authentication.
CJ_USER_ID=pSqmj423mdaHoqZ8GcXyslB5mRN2
